f my favorite kiths<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think you should also turn in your Stormtouched and Iceborn, since they were really cool kiths.<br /> <br /> P.S. I really think you should turn in your Venator, Cursed One, and Hyrophant Kiths, White Oak Dragon. Since they were seriously awesome<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:49:43-08:00","id":1054108,"title":"","content":"I'll have to check first if those last two kiths you mentioned weren't sent yet. But yeah, the Stormtouched and Iceborn are two other favorites of mine.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:55:08-08:00","id":1054113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1054102#post1054102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the info Deionscribe<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I plan to turn in the drafts for my banshee kith since I am very fond of it. I think it is awesome that you turned in your Bramblewright and Wavemaster kiths, since you create some of my favorite kiths<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think you should also turn in your Stormtouched and Iceborn, since they were really cool kiths.<br /> <br /> P.S. I really think you should turn in your Venator, Cursed One, and Hyrophant Kiths, White Oak Dragon. Since they were seriously awesome<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The venator was one of the ones I submitted, after cutting its word count down quite a bit. The Hyrophant isn't one of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:59:37-08:00","id":1054117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1054108#post1054108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to check first if those last two kiths you mentioned weren't sent yet. But yeah, the Stormtouched and Iceborn are two other favorites of mine.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While we are on the subject of your kiths, I want to talk about another of your kiths. I REALLY LIKE your Fury kith, but it is more of a torturer than a vengeance seeking kith. I think you should create a second Fury kith formed from abused women whose power allows them to take vengeance against their abusers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T18:12:28-08:00","id":1054127,"title":"","content":"I don't think you need an altogether new kith for that. In fact, I have a Spellbinder kith whose Blessing can allow them to do something along those lines. Dual Kith it with the Fury, and you have someone who can mete out punishments through a suitable medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:27:36-08:00","id":1055490,"title":"","content":"I am thinking of submitting my banshee kith to see if it can be put in the <i>Hunter's Chronicles </i>rule book. I made some of the changes Deionscribe suggested. Anyone have any more suggestions or ideas? <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Banshee</span></i></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Don\u2019t ever laugh as a hearse goes by, for you may be the next to die.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Being immortals the True Fae are fascinated by death. Not just the concept of being extinguished/ceasing to be, but the emotions surrounding death.To understand death, the True Fae made an agreement with the five original Irish families to exchange one of their daughters who would experience and warn the Irish of an upcoming death. As the Irish intermarried with other races, this list came to include anyone who had an experience with death: Someone who lost a loved one, a survivor of a near death experience, or someone who has to live with the horror of a terminal illness growing in their bodies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Banshee\u2019s Lament:</i></b></span></span> Banshee\u2019s can feel death around them. They see the death marks on mortals and experience a death up to a city block per level of wyrd. Once per scene, if a banshee looks at a target and spends a dot of glamor, that can give them a vision of their death. Any psychic who tries to read the banshee using telepathy or clairvoyance with be forced to experience all the deaths the banshee witnessed. Any any ghost that tries to possess the banshee will be forced to relive the agony of their death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Darkling:</i></b> </span>Ghostly apparitions whose wail foretells your coming death.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Fairest: </i></b></span></span>Na mn\u00e1 fionna</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Wizened: </i></b></span></span>The Washer Woman who cleans your blood stained clothes.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:31:53-08:00","id":1055658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1053579#post1053579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that she intends for them to be submitted using the regular open submissions process, and that if they're interested, they'll hire you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. If you're referring to the post I'm thinking of, what I meant was that kiths would make good writing samples for freelance writing in general, not that we're assembling player-made kiths for publication right now.<br /> <br /> We also won't be hiring for the supplements for a little while yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:51:02-08:00","id":1055665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1055490#post1055490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking of submitting my banshee kith to see if it can be put in the <i>Hunter's Chronicles </i>rule book. I made some of the changes Deionscribe suggested. Anyone have any more suggestions or ideas? <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Banshee</span></i></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Don\u2019t ever laugh as a hearse goes by, for you may be the next to die.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Being immortals the True Fae are fascinated by death. Not just the concept of being extinguished/ceasing to be, but the emotions surrounding death.To understand death, the True Fae made an agreement with the five original Irish families to exchange one of their daughters who would experience and warn the Irish of an upcoming death. As the Irish intermarried with other races, this list came to include anyone who had an experience with death: Someone who lost a loved one, a survivor of a near death experience, or someone who has to live with the horror of a terminal illness growing in their bodies.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Banshee\u2019s Lament:</i></b></span></span> Banshee\u2019s can feel death around them. They see the death marks on mortals and experience a death up to a city block per level of wyrd. Once per scene, if a banshee looks at a target and spends a dot of glamor, that can give them a vision of their death. Any psychic who tries to read the banshee using telepathy or clairvoyance with be forced to experience all the deaths the banshee witnessed. Any any ghost that tries to possess the banshee will be forced to relive the agony of their death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Darkling:</i></b> </span>Ghostly apparitions whose wail foretells your coming death.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Fairest: </i></b></span></span>Na mn\u00e1 fionna</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Wizened: </i></b></span></span>The Washer Woman who cleans your blood stained clothes.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A general thought: I'm not sure how long your kith is, as I'm checking this from my phone and can't easily see word count. That said, they've said before that most kiths are about 250 words long, so if you can edit them down to about that, you could probably submit a few as a single submission. <br /> <br /> On the banshees, you should look them over again. You wouldn't want any extra anys detracting from an otherwise well done submission. I'll need to give a bit more thought to their blessing before I can give proper feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:59:41-08:00","id":1055669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1055658#post1055658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's correct. If you're referring to the post I'm thinking of, what I meant was that kiths would make good writing samples for freelance writing in general, not that we're assembling player-made kiths for publication right now.<br /> <br /> We also won't be hiring for the supplements for a little while yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for confirming that. I expected as much, but I didn't want to ask and become the freelancer equivalent of that kid in the backseat saying &quot;Are we there yet?&quot; every two minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:24:41-08:00","id":1055860,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thanks for the thoughts White Oak Dragon. I really appreciate your feedback<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I agree that the description is too long. I just wanted to find a way to include the myths about the Banshees connection to the five original families of Ireland</span>;</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the O\u2019Grady\u2019s, the O\u2019Neills, the O\u2019Longs, the McCnaimhins, the O\u2019Briens, the O\u2019 Conchobhairs, and the Caomhanachs</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:10:57-08:00","id":1056261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1055860#post1055860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thanks for the thoughts White Oak Dragon. I really appreciate your feedback<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I agree that the description is too long. I just wanted to find a way to include the myths about the Banshees connection to the five original families of Ireland</span>;</span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the O\u2019Grady\u2019s, the O\u2019Neills, the O\u2019Longs, the McCnaimhins, the O\u2019Briens, the O\u2019 Conchobhairs, and the Caomhanachs</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is an interesting story to be sure, but for 2E kiths, even the culturally specific kiths don't usually focus too much on the specific culture in the description. I'd say to go with a bit more of a general description showing how the Fae use them, rather than their historical spread. The touch of what makes the Gentry choose a banshee is a good one, and you should definitely keep that. You would need to make sure that you put the banshees into the same format as the other kiths. I'd also consider changing the Fairest description to make it a bit more evocative. <br /> <br /> On the blessing: Banshees are traditionally known to foresee deaths and warn of them with their keening. As it stands right now, the keening doesn't come up except within the Darkling description. I'd find a way to incorporate the keening into the blessing. The trickiest part is that you'll need to find a way to bring in the death foresight without stomping on the toes of the Oracle kith. Perhaps the banshee can feel death coming in association with those they are bonded with in some way (connected through blood, Merit dots, or oaths, perhaps?). Maybe up to a number of days a way equal to Wyrd provided nothing changes? It would make it a little less useful for detecting violent deaths (given that the individual would be fine until they were badly injured), but good for telling when someone is dying by illness or poison. The keening might be able to fit in by spending a point of Glamour to give everyone with a similar connection to the individual a vision of the person's forthcoming death, giving them a turn of distraction followed by the Spooked Condition or something like that. You could also let them focus it on a specific individual in a more offensive capacity, by which I mean giving a person visions of their own death, not a sonic scream. Maybe in that case the distraction could be a penalty for the next turn equal to half Wyrd, followed by a Condition or Tilt. As the blessing stands now, it seems like it doesn't really have any specific mechanics to it, and rather just lets them automatically win against any psychics or possessing ghosts that target them. Neither of those seem particularly connected to the stories of the banshee, either. Those are just my thoughts on it. You're of course free to do with them what you please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:12:03-08:00","id":1056364,"title":"","content":"Thanks White Oak Dragon<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will give your suggestion considerable thought. I hope you get a chance to work on your Cu Sith, soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:26:48-08:00","id":1056386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1056364#post1056364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks White Oak Dragon<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will give your suggestion considerable thought. I hope you get a chance to work on your Cu Sith, soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. And for what it's worth, I poked around at the Cu Sith a little this morning. I didn't do much with them, but I haven't abandoned them either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:13:39-08:00","id":1056402,"title":"","content":"I am hoping that you can use the Cu Sith to encourage the idea for a Changeling crossover book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:41:32-08:00","id":1056475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1056261#post1056261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is an interesting story to be sure, but for 2E kiths, even the culturally specific kiths don't usually focus too much on the specific culture in the description. I'd say to go with a bit more of a general description showing how the Fae use them, rather than their historical spread. The touch of what makes the Gentry choose a banshee is a good one, and you should definitely keep that. You would need to make sure that you put the banshees into the same format as the other kiths. I'd also consider changing the Fairest description to make it a bit more evocative.<br /> <br /> On the blessing: Banshees are traditionally known to foresee deaths and warn of them with their keening. As it stands right now, the keening doesn't come up except within the Darkling description. I'd find a way to incorporate the keening into the blessing. The trickiest part is that you'll need to find a way to bring in the death foresight without stomping on the toes of the Oracle kith. Perhaps the banshee can feel death coming in association with those they are bonded with in some way (connected through blood, Merit dots, or oaths, perhaps?). Maybe up to a number of days a way equal to Wyrd provided nothing changes? It would make it a little less useful for detecting violent deaths (given that the individual would be fine until they were badly injured), but good for telling when someone is dying by illness or poison. The keening might be able to fit in by spending a point of Glamour to give everyone with a similar connection to the individual a vision of the person's forthcoming death, giving them a turn of distraction followed by the Spooked Condition or something like that. You could also let them focus it on a specific individual in a more offensive capacity, by which I mean giving a person visions of their own death, not a sonic scream. Maybe in that case the distraction could be a penalty for the next turn equal to half Wyrd, followed by a Condition or Tilt. As the blessing stands now, it seems like it doesn't really have any specific mechanics to it, and rather just lets them automatically win against any psychics or possessing ghosts that target them. Neither of those seem particularly connected to the stories of the banshee, either. Those are just my thoughts on it. You're of course free to do with them what you please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your idea of the Banshee's blessing being changed to have keening wail that warns of an individuals upcoming death to all who care/know him. Are there some merits you could recommend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:44:47-08:00","id":1056507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1056475#post1056475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with your idea of the Banshee's blessing being changed to have keening wail that warns of an individuals upcoming death to all who care/know him. Are there some merits you could recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Merits go, Allies and True Friend would be the first ones to come to mind. There's probably some others that could work too, but I can't think of them off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1053577-submitting-kiths?p=1056402#post1056402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping that you can use the Cu Sith to encourage the idea for a Changeling crossover book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Crossover Chronicle is already planned for the future, so I don't think they need my little project to encourage them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 03-01-2017, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:00:07-08:00","id":1056898,"title":"","content":"I am hoping that if your Cu Sith are put in the crossover book, you can be encouraged to develop the concept of Cu Sith who had been captured Forsaken tribe werewolves given to the True Fae by the Pure Tribes or failed Pure tribe wolves given to the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:10:36-08:00","id":1056982,"title":"","content":"Hey White Oak Dragon, Do you have any thoughts on the character summaries I put up on Epic/Legendary Changeling? I might submit them at a later date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}